## Good vs. Bad Examples

### The Headline

❌ **Bad:** Investigation into the Slow Loading Times on the Dashboard Page
✅ **Good:** Dashboard Latency Spikes 400% During Peak Hours

### The "Why It Matters"

❌ **Bad:** It is important to address this because it affects the user experience and could lead to churn which is bad for our Q3 goals.
✅ **Good:** **Business impact:** High latency causes 15% drop-off at checkout. Q3 revenue is at risk.

### By the Numbers

❌ **Bad:**
| Data Point | Value |
|------------|-------|
| Account HQ country | Canada |
| Account HQ state | null |
| Flow failures | 8+ |

✅ **Good:**
| Metric | Before | After |
|--------|--------|-------|
| Error rate | 12% | 0.3% |
| Close time | 45 min | 2 min |

### Technical Detail

❌ **Bad:** (Placed at the top) We looked at the `useEffect` hooks in `dashboard.tsx` and noticed that the dependency array was missing the `userId` variable which caused an infinite loop.
✅ **Good:** (Placed in "Go Deeper") **Root cause:** Infinite loop in `dashboard.tsx`. Missing `userId` in `useEffect` dependency array.
